'''Ty Masterson''' (born September 23, 1969)<ref name=":1">{{cite web | url=https://www.legistorm.com/person/bio/191361/Ty_Masterson.html | title=Kansas State Sen. Ty Masterson - Biography &#124; LegiStorm }}</ref> is an American politician who is the president of the [[Kansas Senate]]. A member of the [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] Party, he has represented the [[Kansas's 16th Senate district|16th district]] since 2009.<ref>[http://www.votesmart.org/summary.php?can_id=57517 Project Vote Smart profile]</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.kanfocus.com/FMPro.php?-DB=House_Profiles_KS&-Lay=Contact&-format=Contact_Senate.html&Name=Ty%20Masterson,%20R-16th&-find|title=KanFocus -- Error}}</ref>  From 2005 to 2008, he was a representative in the [[Kansas House of Representatives]]. He lives in [[Andover, Kansas|Andover]] and served on the Andover City Council. 

Masterson is the [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] nominee in the [[2026 Kansas gubernatorial election]] facing [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] nominee [[Cindy Holscher]].

== Early life and education ==
Masterson was born on September 23, 1969 in [[El Dorado, Kansas]]. He attended [[Kansas State University]] for two years before he dropped out and moved to Wichita, Kansas to start his career as a small [[business owner]], [[contractor]], [[realtor]], and a [[developer]] before he entered [[politics]].<ref name=":1" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-09-24 |title=Ty Masterson |url=https://ballotpedia.org/Ty_Masterson |access-date=2026-10-07 |website=Ballotpedia |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Carpenter |first=Tim |date=2026-09-14 |title=Kansas Republican Ty Masterson concentrates gubernatorial campaign on generational change • Kansas Reflector |url=https://kansasreflector.com/2026/09/14/kansas-republican-ty-masterson-concentrates-gubernatorial-campaign-on-generational-change/ |access-date=2026-10-07 |website=Kansas Reflector |language=en-US}}</ref>

==Committee assignments==
Masterson serves on these [[Kansas State Legislature|legislative committees]]:<ref>[http://www.kslegislature.org/legsrv-senate/searchSenate.do?rep=4465 Profile from the Kansas Legislature]</ref>
* Federal and State Affairs
* Public Health and Welfare
* Utilities

==2026 Kansas gubernatorial campaign==
{{main|2026 Kansas gubernatorial election}}
Masterson is the Republican nominee in the 2026 gubernatorial election in Kansas, and is endorsed by President [[Donald Trump]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Carpenter |first=Tim |date=July 20, 2025 |title=Kansas Senate President Ty Masterson launches Republican campaign for governor |url=https://kansasreflector.com/2025/07/20/kansas-senate-president-ty-masterson-launches-republican-campaign-for-governor/ |access-date=February 16, 2026 |website=[[Kansas Reflector]]}}</ref>

== Personal life ==
Masterson filed for bankruptcy in 2011 after his construction business went under.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kelly |first1=Matthew |url=https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article311074450.html |title=Senate President Ty Masterson wades into crowded Kansas governor’s race |access-date=10 December 2025 |date=July 22, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last1=Sylvester|first1=Ron|title=Andover state senator files for bankruptcy|website=The Wichita Eagle|url=https://www.kansas.com/news/local/article1055219.html}}</ref>

